  Split  jj split -r @ · chain 2 → 1 (2 becomes the parent of 1)                
                                                                                
    1   stays in @                     │   2   file                             
  3 hunks · +3 −2                      │ 1 hunk · +1 −0                         
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────  
  file1.txt                            │ › file                                 
    @@ -10,2 +11,3 @@                  │ ╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌╌  
     line 10                           │ file1.txt                              
    +another line                      │ ▌ @@ -1,3 +1,4 @@                      
  file2.txt                            │ ▌  line 1                              
    @@ -0,0 +1,2 @@                    │ ▌ +new line                            
    +first line                        │ ▌  line 2                              
    +second line                       │                                        
  file3.txt                            │                                        
    @@ -1,3 +0,0 @@                    │                                        
    -deleted line 1                    │                                        
    -deleted line 2                    │                                        
